{"id": "cbe76270-ad31-47a0-995a-ce7bdcce9962", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T10:58:03.332957", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "5decb131-250f-4251-a533-ee45b5cf0e59", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Environment confirmed: no network, no GPU, no torch/transformers, only task.json in /workspace. 224 CPUs, 2TB RAM, 1TB tmpfs.

Now propose the plan skeleton. Keep it structured by points 1-2-3, terse, in Russian (researcher wrote in Russian).

Key design content:

Background from QuaRot (Salehi et al., NeurIPS 2024): Hadamard rotations applied to (a) activation outliers via online Hadamard on activations, (b) weight outliers by rotating weights with random Hadamard before quantization, (c) down_proj of MLP and o_proj handled via pairwise Hadamard "online" transforms to keep computational invariance. Also Chen et al. concurrent work. Key point: QuaRot uses Hadamard transformations to remove outliers, enabling W4A4KV4, and also weight-only quantization (W-only: 4/3/2 bits with FP16 activations/KV). Weight-only results in the paper: QuaRot+GPTQ improves over GPTQ at W3/W2.

Experiment design skeleton:

Models: LLaMA-3-8B, LLaMA-2-7B/13B, Mistral-7B-v0.1, OPT-1.3B/2.7B, and LLaMA-3-70B as stretch (only if resources; probably drop or mark as optional). Also Pythia-2.8b/6.9b for family diversity. Realistic for CPU-only design: they can't run anyway; the design must state compute estimates and feasibility.

Calibration: C4 128 sequences × 2048 tokens (standard GPTQ/QuaRot); alternately WikiText-2 train subset. Fixed seed for sampling.

Tasks/metrics: perplexity on WikiText-2 (context 2048, sequential), C4 held-out; zero-shot accuracy (acc or acc_norm) on LAMBADA, PIQA, HellaSwag, ARC-easy/challenge, WinoGrande, TruthfulQA? Standard lm-eval-harness set; average accuracy. Downstream tasks fixed across conditions.

Conditions:
- FP16 reference.
- RTN W∈{4,3,2} (group sizes 128, and g=-1 per-channel).
- GPTQ W∈{4,3,2} g=128.
- QuaRot+RTN, QuaRot+GPTQ, W∈{4,3,2} g=128.
- Ablations:
  A. Rotation placement: (1) weight-only rotation (offline Hadamard on weights of all layers), (2) +online activation Hadamard (invariance-preserving pairs), (3) only attention/only MLP sub-blocks, (4) skip final head / embeddings.
  Actually the question asked: "убирать ли Hadamard на входах/выходах только или с весами" — i.e., activation-side (online) vs weight-side (offline) rotations. Design a factorial: {no rot, weight-side only, activation-side only, both}.
  B. Group size: g ∈ {-1(per-channel), 128, 64, 32} at W2/W3 to disentangle outlier-removal benefit from granular quantization.
  C. Rotation type: random Hadamard vs deterministic Hadamard (H_2^{⊗k}) vs random permutation (channel shuffle) vs identity — mechanism control. Also multiple random seeds per rotation to see variance of rotation draws (QuaRot notes randomness matters).
  D. Outlier statistics as explanation metric: kurtosis / max-to-mean ratio of per-channel weight and activation magnitudes before/after rotation; count of channels exceeding μ+4σ; correlation between outlier reduction and PPL improvement. This is the mechanism test.
- Optional: QuaRot+GPTQ with different quantization order/act-order, but keep fixed across conditions.

Controls: identical calibration data/seed, identical group size/symmetry(round-to-nearest, asymmetric min-max per group), identical eval set & context length, single shared harness, seeds for GPTQ damping (0.01) and rotation randomness; report mean±std over 3 rotation seeds where randomness applies; deterministic eval.

Success criteria:
- At W4: QuaRot+GPTQ within ~0.1-0.3 PPL of GPTQ (both near-FP16) — i.e., no degradation; expect small or neutral.
- At W3: QuaRot+GPTQ recovers ≥50% of the GPTQ-vs-FP16 PPL gap; average zero-shot accuracy ≥ GPTQ +1 pt.
- At W2: decisive — RTN/GPTQ at W2 g=128 typically collapse (PPL >> baseline, accuracy ≈ chance, e.g., ~25-30 on 4-choice, PPL 10^3+). Success = QuaRot keeps PPL bounded (e.g., < 10× FP16 PPL, or < 100) and average zero-shot accuracy > chance + 5 pts, and strictly better than both baselines by a wide margin. Failure = accuracy at chance regardless.
- Mechanism success: outlier metric reduction (e.g., weight kurtosis drop) correlates with PPL gain (Spearman ρ) across layers/models.

Feasibility/budget without GPU: environment is design-only; no runs possible/claimed. Estimate: GPTQ quantization of 7-8B on 1×A100-80GB ≈ 0.5-2 h; eval PPL + 6 zero-shot tasks ≈ 1-3 h per checkpoint → ~4 h per condition per model. Count conditions: 3 bits × (RTN, GPTQ, QuaRot+RTN, QuaRot+GPTQ) = 12 + FP16 = 13 per model; core model set 2 models → 26 runs ≈ 100-150 GPU·h; ablations ~+150 GPU·h. Total ≈ 250-300 A100·h ≈ manageable but not CPU. CPU-only feasible subset: a scale-free diagnostic — simulate rotation effect on weight statistics and mock quantization error (MSE, Hadamard cost via numpy) — doable in minutes on 224 CPUs without the LLM; that's the only "executable check" for mechanism plausibility (weight outlier statistics require actual weights, so even that needs model downloads → no network). So explicitly: zero executed experiments in this environment; the only feasible checks are paper-based/analytic.

